          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "cursorSync": "Off",
    "description": "Manhattan's 22,324 buildings raised to their roof heights, and the subway as Kepler Plus pipelines floating over them, each service on its own floor with comets running its length.",
    "editable": true,
    "elements": {
      "panel-1": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "id": 1,
          "links": [],
          "title": "",
          "transparent": true,
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "# Manhattan, by height and by subway, in 3D\n\nTwo open datasets and one question: how much of Manhattan is actually within\nwalking distance of a train?\n\nThe buildings are NYC Open Data's footprints — 22,324 across Lower and Midtown,\neach with a surveyed roof height and a year of construction. The subway is the\nMTA's own open data: 29 services and 496 stations, with step-free access marked\non each. Both come from a public [GeoLens](https://datasets.geolibre.app)\ncatalogue, read by DuckDB on the server through the gateway's cache.\n\nWhat this version adds is the subway in the air:\n\n- **Every service is a pipeline on its own floor.** *Subway lines at* sets the\n  height of the lowest; each trunk is 20 m above the one before, and each\n  service 5 m above the one before it in its trunk, so the A, C and E run one\n  over the other along 8th Avenue. The colours are the MTA's.\n- **The comets are the trains.** Expresses run twice as fast as locals, the\n  shuttles at half pace.\n- **Stations stand under their lines**, on the floor of the first service\n  they list, coloured by step-free access.\n\nAs in the original:\n\n- **Press play on the map's clock.** Every building carries its year, so the\n  timeline runs from 1719 to today and the city rises as it plays.\n- **The years belong to the lot, not to the tower.** `construction_year`\n  records the earliest structure on the site, not the one measured here.\n- **The areas are measured in UTM 18N**, not from the file's Web Mercator\n  `shape_area`, which at this latitude inflates them by about 74 %.\n\nThe radius, the floor on height and the eras are dashboard variables: the\ncoverage figure, the table and the map all move together.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-2": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "duckdb"
                      },
                      "group": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "format": 1,
                        "rawQuery": true,
                        "rawSql": "SELECT\n  bin,\n  height_roof AS height_ft,\n  height_roof * 0.3048 AS height_m,\n  era,\n  construction_year,\n  -- The map's clock. Years before 1600 are the file's way of saying \"no idea\",\n  -- and a NULL keeps those buildings out of the animation rather than parking\n  -- them all on one impossible date.\n  CASE WHEN construction_year \u003e= 1600\n       THEN make_timestamp(construction_year, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0) END AS time,\n  round(ST_Area(ST_Transform(geometry, 'EPSG:4326', 'EPSG:32618', always_xy := true))) AS footprint_m2,\n  ST_AsText(geometry) AS geom\nFROM read_parquet('http://feeds/geolens/datasets/4a0bd0db-cd92-424a-8a2e-62d270ae918a.parquet')\nWHERE height_roof \u003e= CAST($minHeight AS DOUBLE)\n    AND era IN (${era:singlequote})"
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "A"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "duckdb"
                      },
                      "group": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "format": 1,
                        "rawQuery": true,
                        "rawSql": "-- Each service once, as the line it runs, on a floor of its own: $lineBase\n-- metres up, 20 m more for each trunk and 5 m more within it, so services\n-- that share a corridor run one above the other. Expresses pace faster.\nWITH floor(service, trunk, metres) AS (\n  VALUES\n    ('1', '1 2 3', 0),\n    ('2', '1 2 3', 5),\n    ('3', '1 2 3', 10),\n    ('4', '4 5 6', 20),\n    ('5', '4 5 6', 25),\n    ('5 Peak', '4 5 6', 30),\n    ('6', '4 5 6', 35),\n    ('7', '7', 40),\n    ('A', 'A C E', 60),\n    ('C', 'A C E', 65),\n    ('E', 'A C E', 70),\n    ('B', 'B D F M', 80),\n    ('D', 'B D F M', 85),\n    ('F', 'B D F M', 90),\n    ('M', 'B D F M', 95),\n    ('G', 'G', 100),\n    ('J', 'J Z', 120),\n    ('Z', 'J Z', 125),\n    ('L', 'L', 140),\n    ('N', 'N Q R W', 160),\n    ('Q', 'N Q R W', 165),\n    ('R', 'N Q R W', 170),\n    ('W', 'N Q R W', 175),\n    ('SF', 'Shuttles', 180),\n    ('SR', 'Shuttles', 185),\n    ('ST', 'Shuttles', 190),\n    ('SIR', 'SIR', 200)\n)\nSELECT\n  l.service,\n  any_value(l.service_name) AS service_name,\n  f.trunk,\n  CAST($lineBase AS DOUBLE) + f.metres AS altitude,\n  CASE WHEN any_value(l.service_name) LIKE '%Express%' THEN 2\n       WHEN f.trunk = 'Shuttles' THEN 0.5 ELSE 1 END AS pace,\n  ST_AsText(ST_Simplify(ST_Collect(list(l.geometry)), 0.00005)) AS geom\nFROM read_parquet('http://feeds/geolens/datasets/fd3a8635-1f38-4b51-a18f-784ea84abbbf.parquet') l JOIN floor f USING (service)\nGROUP BY l.service, f.trunk, f.metres"
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "B"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "duckdb"
                      },
                      "group": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "format": 1,
                        "rawQuery": true,
                        "rawSql": "-- Stations, each on the floor of the first trunk it serves, so a station\n-- stands under its lines whatever height they run at.\nWITH floor(service, trunk, metres) AS (\n  VALUES\n    ('1', '1 2 3', 0),\n    ('2', '1 2 3', 5),\n    ('3', '1 2 3', 10),\n    ('4', '4 5 6', 20),\n    ('5', '4 5 6', 25),\n    ('5 Peak', '4 5 6', 30),\n    ('6', '4 5 6', 35),\n    ('7', '7', 40),\n    ('A', 'A C E', 60),\n    ('C', 'A C E', 65),\n    ('E', 'A C E', 70),\n    ('B', 'B D F M', 80),\n    ('D', 'B D F M', 85),\n    ('F', 'B D F M', 90),\n    ('M', 'B D F M', 95),\n    ('G', 'G', 100),\n    ('J', 'J Z', 120),\n    ('Z', 'J Z', 125),\n    ('L', 'L', 140),\n    ('N', 'N Q R W', 160),\n    ('Q', 'N Q R W', 165),\n    ('R', 'N Q R W', 170),\n    ('W', 'N Q R W', 175),\n    ('SF', 'Shuttles', 180),\n    ('SR', 'Shuttles', 185),\n    ('ST', 'Shuttles', 190),\n    ('SIR', 'SIR', 200)\n)\nSELECT\n  s.stop_name,\n  s.daytime_routes AS routes,\n  CASE s.ada WHEN 1 THEN 'Full' WHEN 2 THEN 'Partial' ELSE 'None' END AS step_free,\n  s.structure,\n  CAST($lineBase AS DOUBLE) + coalesce(f.metres, 0) AS altitude,\n  ST_Y(ST_Centroid(s.geometry)) AS latitude,\n  ST_X(ST_Centroid(s.geometry)) AS longitude\nFROM read_parquet('http://feeds/geolens/datasets/c646ff35-82eb-442f-a524-efcbb1645023.parquet') s\nLEFT JOIN floor f ON f.service = split_part(s.daytime_routes, ' ', 1)"
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "C"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Colour is the era it went up; height is the surveyed roof, in metres. Press play to watch the city arrive.",
          "id": 2,
          "links": [],
          "title": "Every building, raised to its own height, and the subway above",
